    <DataNode elementId="AT1G65840-MONOMER" textLabel="Probable polyamine oxidase 4" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8H191" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA of Arabidopsis PAO4 was expressed in E. coli and purified. AtPAO4 is a flavoprotein. The recombinant enzyme was shown to specifically convert spermine to spermidine. No enzyme activity was detected with spermidine, putrescine, or N&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;/sup&gt;-acetylspermine. AtPAO4 is the major PAO (polyamine oxidase) isoform expressed in Arabidopsis roots.</Comment>
